{meta: title Why Must I Remain}
{meta: x_lyrics_source bluegrass-lyrics}
{meta: x_lyrics_url https://www.bluegrasslyrics.com/song/why-must-i-remain/}

{start_of_verse}
In my life I’ve known sorrow
I’ve seen love fade away
I’ve had tears from sadness
Like those shed today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
My heart was within me
My sadness my own
My thoughts there were anchored
At rest with my soul
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Then when I met you
I gave you my soul
My heart was between us
No longer my own
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
All that I know of
And all that I am
Is shared now with you
How can I remain
Oh lord if you’re with me
Help me find the strength
My soul lay a-dying
Why must I remain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And now you are dying
Now you are alone
And I must remain here
Though my world  is gone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And I am no longer
My heart has no home
There could be no other, God
Don’t leave me alone
ch., repeat last two lines
{end_of_verse}

